  "text": "Glacors\n​\nIntroduction\nGlacors are profitable monsters that can be fought on or off task effectively, usually for their Slayer collection log items, or due to consistent profit from making  and opening  if fought at the Elder God Wars Dungeon.\nThe ability to be assigned Glacors can be unlocked at any Slayer master after completion of Ritual of the Mahjarrat, which also unlocks access to the Glacor Cave.\n​\nStats\n⬥  level: 1\n⬥ XP per kill: 4,810\n⬥ Optimal kills/hr: ~100\n⬥ Optimal XP/hr: ~481,000\n​\nDesirable drops\n⬥ Steadfast Boots\n⬥ Ragefire Boots\n⬥ Glaiven Boots\n​\nLocation and where to stand\nGlacors can be found at the Elder God Wars Dungeon, Glacor Cave, and Frozen Plateau (Wilderness), but are best killed at the Elder God Wars Dungeon due to dropping  and being generally easier to AFK.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The Glacor Front of the EGWD can be accessed quickly using a boss portal leading to Arch-Glacor.\nThere are two viable spots to kill Glacors, which each having pros and cons:\n​\n\n⬥ This spot allows for the consistent killing of 2 Glacor spawns.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The long spawn time of Glacors can cause a lot of downtime which may cause issues with maintaining \n​\n\n⬥ This spot allows for the consistent killing of 3 Glacor spawns.\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• This location is more gear/luck dependant as maintaining max KPH requires fast killing of the Glacors and good Enduring Glacyte luck.\n⬥ Glacytes further North will be killed by some AoE abilities, which may cause them to drop hard to reach  as well as being less efficient XP per Glacor kill while on task.\n​\n AFK Magic\nMagic is the only viable style to AFK Glacors due to Dragon Breath  and Greater Chain  being able to hit the spawned Glacytes while targetting the Glacor.\n​\nNote: When starting your hour or killing too slow, you may take the aggro of 2 Glacors at once, be sure to click on the one your character can actually attack, as one will be unable to be damaged\n​\n⬥ Pray  and  or \n⬥ Sustain  with  / \n⬥ Ensure  is active.\n​\nPreset Suggestions\n⬥ AFK Magic\n​\n\nAction Bars\n\n⬥ Greater Chain  is required for the 3 Glacor spot.\n​\nExample Kills\nAFK Magic  2 Glacors spot - Youtube Link\nAFK Magic  3 Glacors spot - Youtube Link\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Glacors ​ Introduction Glacors are profitable monsters that can be fought on or off task effectively, usually for their Slayer collection log items, or due to consistent profit from making and opening if fought at the Elder God Wars Dungeon. The ability to be assigned Glacors can be unlocked at any Slayer master after completion of Ritual of the Mahjarrat, which also unlocks access to the Glacor Cave. ​ Stats ⬥ level: 1 ⬥ XP per kill: 4,810 ⬥ Optimal kills/hr: ~100 ⬥ Optimal XP/hr: ~481,000 ​ Desirable drops ⬥ Steadfast Boots ⬥ Ragefire Boots ⬥ Glaiven Boots ​ Location and where to stand Glacors can be found at the Elder God Wars Dungeon, Glacor Cave, and Frozen Plateau (Wilderness), but are best killed at the Elder God Wars Dungeon due to dropping and being generally easier to AFK. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The Glacor Front of the EGWD can be accessed quickly using a boss portal leading to Arch-Glacor. There are two viable spots to kill Glacors, which each having pros and cons: ​ ⬥ This spot allows for the consistent killing of 2 Glacor spawns. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• The long spawn time of Glacors can cause a lot of downtime which may cause issues with maintaining ​ ⬥ This spot allows for the consistent killing of 3 Glacor spawns. ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• This location is more gear/luck dependant as maintaining max KPH requires fast killing of the Glacors and good Enduring Glacyte luck. ⬥ Glacytes further North will be killed by some AoE abilities, which may cause them to drop hard to reach as well as being less efficient XP per Glacor kill while on task. ​ AFK Magic Magic is the only viable style to AFK Glacors due to Dragon Breath and Greater Chain being able to hit the spawned Glacytes while targetting the Glacor. ​ Note: When starting your hour or killing too slow, you may take the aggro of 2 Glacors at once, be sure to click on the one your character can actually attack, as one will be unable to be damaged ​ ⬥ Pray and or ⬥ Sustain with / ⬥ Ensure is active. ​ Preset Suggestions ⬥ AFK Magic ​ Action Bars ⬥ Greater Chain is required for the 3 Glacor spot. ​ Example Kills AFK Magic 2 Glacors spot - Youtube Link AFK Magic 3 Glacors spot - Youtube Link",
